\title{rebelrebel: Fast Maps on 'MapLibre' for Marine Data}
\description{
Interactive maps of parquet files and 'DuckDB' tables, drawn in the browser by 'MapLibre GL JS': vessel tracks, survey stations, gridded effort, depth, relief and contours. The data stay in 'DuckDB' and reach the page as vector tiles, so a map of millions of rows stays fast and its colours, filters and legend change in the page. A map is served from R on the local machine, or written as a folder that opens from its 'index.html' with no R and no network but the base map's. Moved from the R package 'ramb', whose map viewer it was.
